---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Krillion.si">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 prose prose-invert">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Effective Date: October 22, 2026</p>
    <p>
      At Krillion.si, we prioritize player privacy. We do not require registration, login, or personal account creation to enjoy any game mode on our platform.
    </p>
    <h2>Information Collection</h2>
    <p>
      Endless practice checks your typed answers on your device. Your dive history, typed inputs and progress stay in this browser when storage is available. To calculate answer rarity, we send the question ID and accepted canonical answer ID for your first valid answer to each category to our own statistics service. Rejected inputs, spelling drafts and timeouts are not uploaded to this service. Pending accepted IDs are stored locally and retried after connection failures.
    </p>
    <p>The statistics service stores a random browser identifier, accepted question and answer IDs, and submission time. A first-party HttpOnly cookie remembers that identifier for up to one year. Only the first accepted answer per category and identifier counts; later choices do not replace it. Clearing cookies or using another browser can create another identifier, so this is an approximate browser sample, not a count of verified people. Our statistics database does not store your name, email, raw typed answers or IP address. Our hosting provider may process connection information to deliver the website.</p>
    <p>Categories use preset scores until they have at least 50 first valid answers. Aggregate answer frequencies then determine practice scores. Daily scoring snapshots and each dive's saved scores keep results stable during play. Individual browser identifiers are not published.</p>
    <p>We may use web analytics and advertising partners (e.g. Google AdSense) to keep the service free for players worldwide.</p>
    <h2>Cookies & Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits. Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Ads Settings in their browser.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
